# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command tilemap
usage 1   tilemap <space> <addr> <cols> <rows>
usage 2                                 decode <cols>x<rows> tilemap entries starting at <addr>
usage 3                                 as a text grid, one already-formatted label per cell -
usage 4                                 see IDebugTarget.DecodeTilemapEntry for what a label
usage 5                                 means on the current core. Caller supplies the exact base
usage 6                                 address (see BG1SC/etc via `regs`) - this doesn't resolve
usage 7                                 BG-layer-to-tilemap-address mapping itself.

case a grid of entries
target fake
covers 1-7
$ tilemap
out 554
  tilemap <space> <addr> <cols> <rows>
                                decode <cols>x<rows> tilemap entries starting at <addr>
                                as a text grid, one already-formatted label per cell -
                                see IDebugTarget.DecodeTilemapEntry for what a label
                                means on the current core. Caller supplies the exact base
                                address (see BG1SC/etc via `regs`) - this doesn't resolve
                                BG-layer-to-tilemap-address mapping itself.
status 0
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 0
out 554
  tilemap <space> <addr> <cols> <rows>
                                decode <cols>x<rows> tilemap entries starting at <addr>
                                as a text grid, one already-formatted label per cell -
                                see IDebugTarget.DecodeTilemapEntry for what a label
                                means on the current core. Caller supplies the exact base
                                address (see BG1SC/etc via `regs`) - this doesn't resolve
                                BG-layer-to-tilemap-address mapping itself.
status 0
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 0 4 2
out 31
005 1A7 341 4E3
685 827 9C1 B63
status 0
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 10 8 3
out 95
D05 EA7 041 1E3 385 527 6C1 863
A05 BA7 D41 EE3 085 227 3C1 563
705 8A7 A41 BE3 D85 F27 0C1 263
status 0
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 3FC 4 2
out 31
CC1 E63 005 1A7
341 4E3 685 827
status 0
action none
$ tilemap NOPE 0 1 1
out 83
Error: No memory space named 'NOPE'. Available: RAM, ROM, VRAM, IO, UNSIZED, CpuBus
status 1
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 0 0 0
out 0

status 0
action none
$ tilemap VRAM 0 x 1
out 46
Error: Could not find any recognizable digits.
status 1
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ tilemap VRAM 0 1 1
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
end

case on venus
target venus
covers 1
$ tilemap VRAM 0 4 2
out 63
0000... 0000... 0000... 0000...
0000... 0000... 0000... 0000...
status 0
action none
end

case on moon
target moon
covers 1
$ tilemap PPU 0 4 2
out 100
Error: No memory space named 'PPU'. Available: RAM, PRGROM, PRGRAM, CHR, CIRAM, OAM, PALETTE, CPUBUS
status 1
action none
end

case on mercuryrt
target mercuryrt
covers 1
$ tilemap VRAM 0 4 2
out 31
$00 $00 $00 $00
$00 $00 $00 $00
status 0
action none
end

case on nephrite
target nephrite
covers 1
$ tilemap VRAM 0 4 2
out 7
   
   
status 0
action none
end
